Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:28:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 65/65] consensus: set the two P2MR tripwire outputs of the
 Ark-0 signet

ARK0_TRIPWIRE_OUTPOINTS gets the two outputs created on the Ark-0 signet
at height 15748, 10,000 sats each. Both are P2MR outputs of two leaves of
version 0xc0 at depth one, <key> OP_CHECKSIG and OP_RETURN:

- 4319a38c0842846474ff038b54f22aec844147a97c2abc462bfb92957c1bc3a0:1,
  labelled "BIP-341 NUMS", whose key is the NUMS point H of BIP 341
  (XOnlyPubKey::NUMS_H), which no one can spend;
- 8991bb83673474b7c324f303365479c093d0b34f5e7d7ddf0648bcfdb1d42495:0,
  labelled "drill", whose key,
  2f605bb3d127c17ff8e88e214587876b0c7623dbad79f8a1115fa172bda0315f, the
  operator holds, to spend it when the drill is triggered.

ARK0_TRIPWIRE_HEIGHT is set to 30000, so the rules apply on Ark-0 from
that height. A static_assert keeps it above
ARK0_TRIPWIRE_CREATION_HEIGHT, 15748: an output only counts as present
when it was created below the height of the rules. A unit test rebuilds
each output's scriptPubKey from its key and the two leaves and compares
it with the one on that chain.

The heights test checks Ark-0's parameters against the constants, with
the rules enabled exactly when ARK0_TRIPWIRE_HEIGHT is not
std::numeric_limits<int>::max(), so that setting the height changes the
constant, its comment and its sentence in doc/p2mr-tripwire.md only.
